      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "one of the reasons is that the safety settings seem to only look when an avatar is initially loaded what is put on it. Once you fire an animation switching out the material said material is not covered by the safety settings. Already made a bug report about that but it does not seem to get any attention: https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/avatar-30-material-change-breaks-shader-safety-setting\nTLDR:\nif you disable shaders for people, disable animations as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
